### [bind()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-method}

::: {.doc-subject}

Build a `Surv` response from the columns of `data`.
:::

::: {.doc-usage-source}
Usage

[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/greenwood/blob/main/greenwood/_outcome.py#L595-L675){target="_blank" rel="noopener"}
:::

::: {.doc-signature .doc-Kind.FUNCTION}
```python
bind(data)
```
:::

::: {.doc-text}

`bind()` is strict: missing values in the response columns raise an error, as they do in
the `Surv` constructors. To drop incomplete rows automatically, pass the `Outcome` to an
estimator's `fit()` with `data=` instead, where the response and covariates are filtered
together.
:::

#### Parameters {.doc-parameters}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code>[data]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Any]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   A data frame (pandas, Polars, PyArrow, DuckDB, a lazy frame, ...) or a mapping of
    column names to values.
:::

#### Returns {.doc-returns}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code> [Surv]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   The response for this frame.
:::

