### [counting()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-method}

::: {.doc-subject}

Describe a counting-process `(start, stop]` response.
:::

::: {.doc-usage-source}
Usage

[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/greenwood/blob/main/greenwood/_outcome.py#L234-L281){target="_blank" rel="noopener"}
:::

::: {.doc-signature .doc-Kind.FUNCTION}
```python
counting(
    start,
    stop,
    event=None,
    *,
    weights=None,
    event_value=None,
    censor_value=None
)
```
:::

#### Parameters {.doc-parameters}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code>[start]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str | Duration]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   The column holding entry times, or a `duration()`.

<code>[stop]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str | Duration]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   The column holding exit times, or a `duration()` computed from two date columns.

<code>[event]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   The column holding the event indicator. If `None`, every row is an event.

<code>[weights]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   The column holding case weights (optional).

<code>[event_value]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Any]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   The value (or list of values) in `event` that marks an event. See `Surv.counting()`.

<code>[censor_value]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Any]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   The value (or list of values) in `event` that marks censoring. Pass this or
    `event_value`, not both.
:::

#### Returns {.doc-returns}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code> [Outcome]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   A data-free description of the response.
:::

#### Examples {.doc-examples}

::: {#c64427f2 .cell execution_count=7}
``` {.python .cell-code}
import greenwood as gw

gw.Outcome.counting(start="tstart", stop="tstop", event="event")
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=7}
```
Outcome.counting(start='tstart', stop='tstop', event='event')
```
:::
:::


### [first_event()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-method}

::: {.doc-subject}

Describe a competing-risks response built from several endpoint column pairs.
:::

::: {.doc-usage-source}
Usage

[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/greenwood/blob/main/greenwood/_outcome.py#L378-L466){target="_blank" rel="noopener"}
:::

::: {.doc-signature .doc-Kind.FUNCTION}
```python
first_event(endpoints, *, censor_at=None, start=None, weights=None)
```
:::

::: {.doc-text}

Each endpoint has its own time and event column. For each row, the earliest observed event
wins, ties go to the endpoint listed first, and rows with no observed event are censored
at the latest endpoint time (or at `censor_at`). See `Surv.first_event()`.
:::

#### Parameters {.doc-parameters}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code>[endpoints]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Mapping[str, Sequence[Any]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   A mapping of state label to `(time, event)` or `(time, event, event_value)` column
    names, in priority order for ties.

<code>[censor_at]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str | Duration | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   The column holding the censoring time for rows with no observed event (optional).

<code>[start]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str | Duration | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   The column holding entry times, for late entry (optional).

<code>[weights]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   The column holding case weights (optional).
:::

#### Returns {.doc-returns}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code> [Outcome]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   A data-free description of the response.
:::

#### Examples {.doc-examples}

We'll use the bundled `mgus2` dataset, which follows patients with monoclonal gammopathy.
Each endpoint has its own column pair: `ptime` and `pstat` for progression to plasma-cell
malignancy (PCM), and `futime` and `death` for death. Here is what the dataset looks like:

